    {
      "id": "SG-006",
      "name": "Security: Effective Balance Grinding Prevention",
      "description": "By computing the proposer lookahead at the epoch boundary using effective balances frozen at the start of epoch N - MIN_SEED_LOOKAHEAD (rather than the start of epoch N), this EIP removes the ability for validators to manipulate their effective balance after seeing the RANDAO outcome to influence the proposer schedule. This aligns the effective-balance delay with the RANDAO delay, collapsing the security analysis from a subtle examination of EB edge cases to a trivial analysis.",
